# `words(mix)` is handed texts, numbers, booleans and one kind of record. It asks `typeof mix` itself; behind its own tests the value is stepped through by `for (k in mix)` and read under the key: no name is used off it. The program has told the primitives apart already, so what is held of the view is still cut to the record, and the names are stepped through as the record lists them.
# One call passes all of them. (Calls that pass a text or a number each are copied, and the function is left the record alone: it asks for no shape then.)
# f1 = words
# RUN(FORM): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# FORM-LABEL: code f1:Body
# FORM: [[record]]: boolean @Boolean = ShapeTest {{*}} layouts=[L0]
# FORM: = HasKeyOrder {{*}} layout=L0
